  "use_case": "Working capital and cash flow optimization",
  "space_title": "CapitalFlow Machinery - Working Capital Optimization 💰",
  "space_description": "**Scenario:** You're treasurer at CapitalFlow Machinery, staring at a Cash Conversion Cycle stuck near the 120-day high end of the industrial band while the CEO presses you to free trapped cash for capex. DSO is drifting past the 45-day target in parts of the business and collections are uneven. Where is cash trapped longest, and which business units are letting receivables age?\n\n**Questions:**\n\n1. Showcase the different visualization options with interesting aspects of the dataset (agent)\n2. What is my working capital position by business unit type, with average DSO, DPO, and cash conversion cycle for each? (agent)\n3. Which 10 business units have the longest Cash Conversion Cycle, and how do their DSO and outstanding AR balances compare? (agent)",
  "schema_basename": "mach_working_capital",
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "cash_flow_transactions",
      "description": "Cash inflow and outflow transaction records.",
      "columns": [
