  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports working capital and cash flow optimization at CapitalFlow. Stakeholders: Treasurer and AR/AP teams (collections, payment timing, aging buckets), CFO (CCC, NWC, OCF/FCF, forecast variance), and CEO (capital efficiency, capex/dividend coverage, balance-sheet discipline across business units).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Cash Conversion Cycle = AVG(cash_conversion_cycle_days) = DSO + DIO − DPO; leaders <60 days.\n- DSO = AVG(dso_days); target <45 days for B2B industrials.\n- DPO = AVG(dpo_days); 45–75 days leverages float without supplier risk.\n- Net Working Capital = SUM(working_capital_usd); minimize subject to growth needs.\n- Operating cash flow = SUM(operating_cash_flow_usd); core business cash generation.\n- Free cash flow = SUM(free_cash_flow_usd); OCF − capex; funds dividends and buybacks.\n- Collection rate = AVG(collection_rate_pct); target ≥98%.\n- Forecast variance = AVG(forecast_variance_pct); accuracy target <5%.\n- Note on direction vs txn_type: `direction` (Inflow / Outflow) is generated independently of `txn_type` in synthetic data, so do not assume a strict business mapping (e.g. AR Collection is not always Inflow). When you need true inflow/outflow semantics, filter on `direction` rather than inferring it from `txn_type`.\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - cash_flow_txn_metrics (source: cash_flow_transactions) — dims: txn_date, business_unit_type, txn_type, direction; measures: total_inflow, total_outflow, total_transactions, avg_days_outstanding, unique_business_unit_count, max_amount.\n  - cash_flow_kpi_metrics (source: cash_flow_monthly) — dims: kpi_month, business_unit_type; measures: total_net_cash_flow, total_operating_cf, avg_collection_rate, total_working_capital, total_free_cash_flow, total_forecast_variance_percent.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. business_unit_id, dso_days, dpo_days, cash_conversion_cycle_days, accounts_receivable_usd, accounts_payable_usd).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
